menu "System Data Connector Options"
    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_MAX
        int "Maximum Connectors in Registry"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
          Maximum number of data connectors in the system registry.

    config SYS_DATA_PROVIDER_MAX
        int "Maximum Providers in Registry"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
          Maximum number of transport providers in the registry.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_PROVIDERS_MAX
        int "Maximum Providers per Connector (TX/RX)"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          Maximum number of providers that can be attached to a single connector
          for fan-out (TX) or fan-in (RX).

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_NAME_MAX
        int "Maximum Connector Name Length"
        default 16
        range 8 64
        help
          Maximum length of diagnostic name string per connector.

    config SYS_DATA_CONNECTOR_FRAME_MAX
        int "Maximum Frame Length (bytes)"
        default 512
        range 64 4096
        help
          Largest frame any connector carries in either direction, including
          the outbound stream byte. Every frame buffer on the path (connector
          send, sys_interface RX, recorded actions) is statically sized to it.
          The limit used at runtime is smaller when a transport reports one
          (BLE: the negotiated MTU - 3); see sys_data_connector_max_payload().
endmenu
